message.content:
{
  "action": "send",
  "subject": "HN annual agreement: turning faster cash into price",
  "body": "Dear Thomas,\n\nThank you for recognising the data and timing points. You are right that iron and wages remain pressures; I understand that punctual, faster cash makes Package A your strongest basis. Your costing can remain internal.\n\nBecause [[c10]] we can back that outlook with the agreed 8,150-piece annual quantity, which is why we ask for a further price improvement.\n\nAlso, [[c8]] which supports keeping a simple fixed-price year rather than introducing further uncertainty.\n\nIf you can agree EUR 128.85 from 1 November, we can move up from EUR 124.98 and commit to 14-day payment, reliably on time, for the 12-month agreement.\n\nAs a timing probe, we could instead offer EUR 132.14 from 1 April with the same 14-day payment and annual quantity.\n\nHow close can you bring the early-payment package to EUR 128.85?\n\nHollerau Pumpenwerke, Purchasing",
  "term_sheets": [
    {
      "unit_price": 128.85,
      "effective_date": "2026-11-01",
      "payment_days": 14
    },
    {
      "unit_price": 132.14,
      "effective_date": "2027-04-01",
      "payment_days": 14
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Thomas explicitly values Package A, but his April offer has the lower estimated total cost. The main proposal trades a conditional price concession for reliable early payment, while the single probe combines that cash benefit with the later effective date.",
  "target_price": 128.85
}

